$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a suspension of 2-(2-methylamino-ethyl)-isoindole-1,3-dione (3.56g,
14.8 mmoles) in dichloromethane (1.6 mL) was added
2-(pyridin-3-yl)thiazole-5-carbaldehyde (190 mg, 1.00 mmol), sodium
triacetoxyborohydride (741 mg, 3.32 mmol), and acetic acid (0.764 mL,
1.33 mmol). The reaction mixture was left stirring at room temperature
for 4 hours saturated aqueous sodium bicarbonate was added (20 mL), and
the mixture was extracted with dichloromethane (100 mL). The organic
phase was dried over Na2SO4, filtered and concentrated. The crude product
was purified by flash chromatography (1:1:1 hexanes:ethyl acetate:
dichloromethane) to yield
2-(2-(methyl((2-(pyridin-3-yl)thiazol-5-yl)methyl)amino)ethyl)isoindoline-1,3-dione,
yield 410 mg, 100%. MH+(379).
