suspension of rotaxane 1 (49 mg, 50 μmol), sodium
tri(benzoyloxy)borohydride 5f (0.16 g, 0.75 mmol), and triethylamine
(0.14 mL, 1.0 mmol) in dry NMP (0.5 mL) was heated to 70 °C for 16 h.
After cooling to r.t., 5 mL of water was added to the mixture and the
aqueous mixture was extracted three times with chloroform (10 mL). The
combined organic layer was dried over MgSO4 and concentrated under
reduced pressure. The residue was purified by short column chromatography
(aluminium oxide, EtOAc) to afford quantitative recovering of 1 (Table 2,
entry 9): In the above procedure, 5f (74 mg, 0.25 mmol) and benzaldehyde
6f (0.05 mL, 0.5 mmol) were used to afford 2f (100% conversion).
Highly-pure 2f was obtained by recrystallization from
chloroform/2-propanol (24 mg, 26 μmol, 52%). m.p. 187.1-187.3 °C; 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3, 298 K) δ 8.17 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 8.09 (s, 2H), 7.33
(d, J = 7.1 Hz, 2H), 7.23 (d, J = 7.1 Hz, 2H), 7.20-7.19 (m, 3H), 7.06
(s, 1H), 6.95 (s, 2H), 6.89-6.81 (m, 9H), 5.98 (s, 2H), 4.10-4.04 (m,
8H), 3.71-3.64 (m, 8H), 3,44 (s, 2H), 3.40 (s, 4H), 3.25-3.20 (m, 4H),
2.87-2.83 (m, 4H), 2.27 (s, 6H), 2.18 (s, 6H) ppm; 13C NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3, 298 K) δ 167.2, 148.6, 140.2, 139.9, 137.7, 137.5, 136.8, 136.1,
134.1, 130.9, 128.8, 128.4, 128.3, 128.2, 128.1, 126.7, 126.7, 120.5,
111.5, 69.6, 69.2, 68.0, 67.0, 57.9, 57.7, 57.6, 21.5, 20.9 ppm; IR (KBr)
ν 2923 (νC-H, as), 2875 (νC-H, as), 1710 (νC=O as), 1505 (νC=C, as), 1216
(νC(=O)-O-C, as), 1053 (νC-O-C, as) cm-1; FAB-HR-MS calcd for C57H68NO10
[M+H]+ 926.4843, found 926.4845.
