$DATUM Synthesis of N-propylated rotaxane 2b: (Table 2, entry 1) In a screw cap
tube a solution of rotaxane 1 (49 mg, 50 µmol), sodium
tri(propionyloxy)borohydride 5b (0.16 g, 0.75 mmol), and triethylamine
(0.14 mL, 1.0 mmol) in dry NMP (0.5 mL) was heated to 70 °C for 16 h.
After cooling to r.t., 5 mL of water was added to the mixture and the
aqueous mixture was extracted three times with chloroform (10 mL). The
combined organic layer was dried over MgSO4 and concentrated under
reduced pressure. The residue was purified by short column chromatography
(aluminium oxide, EtOAc) and recrystallized from chloroform /2-propanol
to give 2b (100% conversion, isolated: 26 mg, 0.03 mmol, 60%) as a
colorless solid. m.p. 121.0-121.3 °C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3, 298 K) δ
8.12 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 8.09 (s, 2H), 7.12 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 7.06
(s, 1H), 6.92 (s, 2H), 6.89-6.81 (m, 9H), 5.99 (s, 2H), 4.10-4.04 (m,
8H), 3.71-3.64 (m, 8H), 3,41 (s, 2H), 3.40 (s, 2H), 3.25-3.21 (m, 4H),
2.91-2.87 (m, 4H), 2.27 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 2.27 (s, 6H), 2.18 (s, 6H),
1.47-1.42 (m, 2H), 0.79 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 3H) ppm; 13C NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3,
298 K) δ 167.04, 148.5, 140.2, 137.5, 137.3, 136.9, 136.1, 134.0, 129.8,
128.5, 128.2, 128.1, 128.0, 126.5, 120.4, 111.4, 69.4, 69.1, 67.8, 66.9,
58.1, 57.9 55.09, 21.3, 20.8, 20.0, 11.9 ppm; IR (KBr) ν 2920 (νC-H, as),
2871 (νC-H, as), 1715 (νC=O as), 1505 (νC=C, as), 1219 (νC(=O)-O-C, as),
1054 (νC-O-C, as) cm-1; FAB-HR-MS calcd for C53H68NO10 [M+H]+ 878.4843,
found 878.4843.
