$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of N-cyclohexylmethylated rotaxane 2d: (Table 2, entry 2) In a
screw cap tube a solution of rotaxane 1 (49 mg, 50 µmol), sodium
tri(cyclohexanecarbonyloxy)borohydride 5d (0.16 g, 0.75 mmol), and
triethylamine (0.14 mL, 1.0 mmol) in dry NMP (0.5 mL) was heated to 70 °C
for 40 h. After cooling to r.t., 5 mL of water was added to the mixture
and the aqueous mixture was extracted three times with chloroform (10
mL). The combined organic layer was dried over MgSO4 and concentrated
under reduced pressure. The residue was purified by short column
chromatography (aluminium oxide, EtOAc) and recrystallized from
chloroform /2-propanol to give 2d (100% conversion, isolated: 37 mg, 40
µmol, 79%) as a colorless solid. m.p. 187.5-188.5 °C; 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3, 298 K) δ 8.14 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 8.10 (s, 2H), 7.12 (d, J = 8.0
Hz, 2H), 7.06 (s, 1H), 6.92 (s, 2H), 6.89-6.81 (m, 9H), 5.99 (s, 2H),
4.10-4.04 (m, 8H), 3.71-3.64 (m, 8H), 3.36 (s, 4H), 3.25-3.21 (m, 4H),
2.91-2.87 (m, 4H), 2.27 (s, 6H), 2.18 (s, 6H), 2.08 (d, J = 7.4 Hz, 2H),
1.81-1.78 (m, 2H), 1.65-1.61 (m, 2H), 1.59-1.50 (m, 1H), 1.19-1.12 (m,
4H), 0.87-0.66 (m, 2H) ppm; 13C NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3, 298 K) δ 167.2,
148.3, 140.4, 137.7, 137.4, 137.3, 136.2, 134.1, 130.9, 128.6, 128.4,
128.2, 128.1, 126.6, 120.5, 111.5, 69.6, 69.3, 68.0, 67.1, 60.5, 58.7,
58.6, 35.6, 31.8, 27.1, 26.4, 21.5, 20.9 ppm; IR (KBr) ν 2925 (νC-H, as),
1710 (νC=O as), 1504 (νC=C, as), 1216 (νC(=O)-O-C, as), 1054 (νC-O-C, as)
cm-1; FAB-HR-MS calcd for C57H74NO10 [M+H]+ 932.5313, found 932.5329.
