$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of N-methyl rotaxane 2h4: (Table 2, entry 13) In a screw cap
tube a suspension of rotaxane 1 (49 mg, 50 μmol), paraformaldehyde (15
mg, 0.5 mmol), sodium triacetoxyborohydride 5a (0.16 g, 0.75 mmol), and
triethylamine (0.14 mL, 1.0 mmol) in dry NMP (0.5 mL) was heated to 70 °C
for 16 h. After cooling to r.t., 5 mL of water was added to the mixture
and the aqueous mixture was extracted three times with chloroform (10
mL). The combined organic layer was dried over MgSO4 and concentrated
under reduced pressure. The residue was purified by short column
chromatography (aluminium oxide, EtOAc) to afford 2h (100% conversion,
isolated:32 mg, 38 μmol, 75%) as a colorless solid. 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3, 298 K) δ 8.14-8.11 (m, 4H), 7.12 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 7.06 (s,
1H), 6.91-6.82 (m, 10H), 6.02 (s, 2H), 4.10-4.04 (m, 8H), 3.74-3.64 (m,
8H), 3,41 (s, 2H), 3.34 (s, 2H), 3.28-3.25 (m, 4H), 2.95-2.92 (m, 4H),
2.28 (s, 6H), 2.19 (s, 6H), 2.09 (s, 3H) ppm. Lit: 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 8.13-8.10 (m, 4H), 7.11 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 7.06 (s, 2H),
6.90-6.81 (m, 10H), 6.00 (s, 2H), 4.11-4.03 (m, 8H), 3.73-3.64 (m, 8H),
3.41 (s, 2H), 3.34 (s,2H), 3.28-3.24 (m, 4H), 2.27 (s, 6H), 2.18 (s, 6H),
2.09 (s, 3H) ppm.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM paraformaldehyde used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Selective Transformation of a Crown Ether/sec-Ammonium Salt-Type Rotaxane
to N-Alkylated Rotaxanes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Suzuki, Sakiko; Nakazono, Kazuko; Takata, Toshikazu
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2010), 12(4), 712-715

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME17 STEP1
$RXN



