$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (Py)(Trz)2,9 (Eq. S6). Pyridine carboxaldehyde
(0.107 g, 1 mmol) was dissolved in 1,2-DCE (4 mL) and to it was added
(Trz)2NH (0.359, 1 mmol), followed by brief sonication. Na[BH(OAc)3]
(95%, 0.335 g, 1.5 mmol) was poured in and the reaction mixture was
stirred at room temperature overnight. The yellow reaction was quenched
with NaHCO3/ NaOH and diluted with CH2Cl2, while maintaining the aqueous
pH 8-9. The product was extracted with dichloromethane (3 × 20 mL), the
combined organic layers were washed with H2O, dried over anhydrous MgSO4,
filtered and concentrated under vacuum. (Py)(Trz)2 (9), orange waxy solid
(0.450 g, 99%). ESI-MS: m/z 451.2 (M+H+), 473.2 (M+Na+). 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 8.48 (dm, J = 4.9 Hz, 1H), 7.61 - 7.56 (m, 1 H), 7.59 (s, 2H),
7.47 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 7.33 - 7.28 (m, 6H), 7.24 - 7.20 (m, 4H), 7.10
(ddd, J = 7.8, 4.9, 1.1 Hz 1H), 5.47 (s, 4H), 3.76 (s, 2H), 3.75 (s, 4H).
13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ 158.90, 148.98, 144.52, 136.64, 134.87,
129.09, 128.66, 128.00, 123.70, 123.48, 122.14, 59.17, 54.08, 47.85.
