pale-green oil (1.795 g). 2-(4’-fluorobenzylamino)ethanol (48d). The
procedure to prepare 48d is the same as that to prepare 48a except using
4-fluorobenzaldehyde (1.241 g, 0.01 mmol) instead of
4-chlorobenzaldehyde. The desired product was purified by column
chromatography (silica gel, CH2Cl2 : MeOH = 9.25 : 0.75) to afford a
pale-green oil (1.623 g, 96%). 1H NMR (CDCl3, 500 MHz): δ 7.276-7.249 (m,
2H), 7.014-6.890 (m, 2H), 3.745 (s, 2H), 3.632 (t, 2H, J=5Hz), 2.747 (t,
2H, J=4Hz), 2.623 (brs, 2H). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 125.7 MHz): δ
(163.079+161.130) (1C), (135.709+135.691) (1C), (129.905+129.845) (2C),
(115.461+115.298) (2C), 60.922 (1C), 52.987 (1C), 50.759 (1C). MS (ESI,
CH3OH): [C9H12FNO] m/z 170.5 ([M+H]+); m/z 361.6 ([2M+Na]+).
