$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1'-Benzyl-[1,4']bipiperidinyl-2-one (11): To a 1-L, 3-necked,
round-bottom flaskequipped with an overhead mechanical stirrer,
thermocouple probe, solid addition funnel,and a dynamic nitrogen inlet
were added 5-aminovaleric acid hydrochloride (22.32 g,0.145 mol),
1-benzyl-4-piperidone (11.0 g, 0.058 mol) and anhydrous
1,2-dichloroethane(220 mL). To this stirring solution was added
NaBH(OAc)3 (18.5 g, 0.087 mol) in four portions over a one-hour period.
The flask was aged at room temperature for 30 minutes.The solid addition
funnel was exchanged for a liquid addition funnel and triethylamine (14.7
g, 0.145 mol) was added over a 15-minute period. The flask was aged at
roomtemperature for 14 hours then heated to 60 °C for 60 additional
hours. The solution wascooled to room temperature and quenched by the
slow addition of water (250 mL). The reaction was treated in an analogous
fashion to Method A to yield 1'-benzyl-[1,4']bipiperidinyl-2-one (11)
(14.2 g, 92% yield) as a pale yellow solid after recrystallization from
heptane (~10 mL/gram). On small scale (1.0 gram), Method B has also been
shown to produce compound 11. In this instance, the reaction was aged
atroom temperature for 24 hours then heated to reflux for 24 additional
hours. After recrystallization, yielded
1'-benzyl-[1,4']bipiperidinyl-2-one (11) as a pale yellow solid, yield
1.13 g, 52% . 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.33-7.22 (m, 5H), 4.54 (tt, J =
12.2 Hz, J = 4.1 Hz,1H), 3.49 (s, 2H), 3.19 (t, J = 5.7 Hz, 2H),
2.94-2.91 (m, 2H), 2.39 (t = 6.1 Hz, 2H), 2.11(dt, J = 11.8 Hz, J = 2.3
Hz, 2H), 1.79-1.69 (m, 6H), 1.58-1.55 (m, 2H). 13C NMR(100MHz, CDCl3):
δ169.43, 138.37, 129.14, 128.19, 127.00, 63.03, 52.94, 50.43,
41.85,32.60, 28.54, 23.35, 20.87. IR (neat) 1625, 1489, 1457, 1444, 1352,
1323, 1270, 1168,1122, 788, 736, 696, 659, 613 cm-1. Anal. Calcd (found):
C, 74.96 (75.06); H, 8.88(9.04); N, 10.28 (9.98). MS (electrospray):
exact mass calcd for C17H24N2O 272.1889;m/z found, 273.1972 [M+H]+; mp
77.3 °C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
