$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of 3(R)-1,3-dibenzyl-4-(2,2-dimethylpropanoyl)piperazin-2-one
(6d). To a 0 °C stirring suspension of D-phenylalanine methyl ester
hydrochloride (100 mg, 0.464 mmol, 1.0 equiv.), 4Å powdered molecular
sieves (200 mg), acetic acid (80 μL, 1.4 mmol, 3.0 equiv.) and sodium
triacetoxyborohydride (148 mg, 0.696 mmol, 1.5 equiv.) in 5 mL
acetonitrile was added dropwise over 5 minutes a 2.5 mL acetonitrile
solution of aldehyde 4d (119 mg, 0.510 mmol, 1.1 equiv.). After stirring
for 90 minutes, the ice bath was removed and the reaction was warmed to
ambient temperature and stirred for 18 hours. The pressure tube was
sealed and heated to 120 °C for 48 hours. The mixture was cooled and
poured into aqueous saturated NaHCO3, which was extracted three times
with dichloromethane. The combined organic extracts were dried (Na2SO4),
filtered and concentrated in vacuo. Purification by flash chromatography
(0 to 60% ethyl acetate in hexanes) provided piperazinone 6d as clear oil
(156 mg, 92% yield). Chiral HPLC analysis (Chiralcel OD column 250 X 4.6
mm; 220 nm; flow = 1.0 mL/minute of A/B:80/20 (A=hexanes, B=2-propanol);
30 minute run. 26.8% enantiomeric excess. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ
7.35-7.27 (m, 3H), 7.25-7.24 (m, 3H), 7.24-7.17 (m, 4H), 5.28 (t, J = 5.0
Hz, 1H), 4.99 (d, J = 14.6 Hz, 1H), 4.26 (d, J = 14.6 Hz, 1H), 3.89 (br
d, J = 12.7 Hz, 1H), 3.51 (dd, J = 13.7, 5.1 Hz, 1H), 3.28 (dd, J = 13.5,
5.5 Hz, 1H), 3.23 (td, J = 11.8, 3.9 Hz, 1H), 2.87 (dt, J = 12.0, 2.5 Hz,
1H), 2.59 (br t, J = 11.3 Hz, 1H), 1,18 (s, 9H).HRMS (ES) exact mass
calculated for C23H29N2O2 (M+H+): 365.2224; found 365.2202.Retention time
for 6d = 11.0 minutes (Area % = 58.28), enantiomer retention time = 14.8
minutes (Area % = 33.64);
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM mol. sieves used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Preparation of Substituted Piperazinones via Tandem Reductive
Amination-(N,N'-Acyl Transfer)-Cyclization
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Beshore, Douglas C.; Dinsmore, Christopher J.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2002), 4(7), 1201-1204

