$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the condensation of 8
with 12 to prepare 9. Compound 8, 12, and sodium triacetoxyborohydride
were mixed in a ratio of 1.1/1/1.5 in 1,2-dichloroethane and 1 equivalent
of acetic acid was added. The mixture was stirred under argon at room
temperature for 12-16 h and treated with 1N NaOH to pH>12. The expected
product was extracted with ethyl acetate. The extract was washed with
brine, dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, and evaporated to give crude product,
which was purified by flash chromatography on silica gel (yield: 50 -
90%). Scheme 1a, 9, yield 90%
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
