$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Tetracyclic secondary amine 26 : Sodium triacetoxyborohydride (50 mg,
0.237 mmol) and glacial acetic acid (4 drops from 22G needle) was added
to a solution of aldehyde 25 (47 mg, 0.169 mmol) and amine 24 (as the TFA
salt, 52 mg, 0.0169 mmol) in methylene chloride (2 mL). After 24 hours,
saturated sodium bicarbonate was added and extracted with ethyl acetate
several times. The combined organic extracts were dried over Na2SO4,
filtered and concentrated. The crude product was purified by silica gel
chromatography (50% EtOAc/Hx) to afford secondary amine 26 (70 mg, 90%)
as a pale yellow oil. [α]D (MeOH) = -56°; IR (film, cm-1): 3354, 2922,
2852, 1735, 1693, 1436, 1366, 1259, 1169, 1140, 1073, 1053, 992, 928; 1H
NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 6.20 (d, J = 10.6 Hz, 1H), 6.11 (m, 2H), 5.98 (m,
2H), 5.70 (m, 1H), 5.33 (m, 2H), 5.23 (t, J = 11.0, 2H), 4.70 (m, 3H),
4.34 (m, 2H), 4.11 (d, J = 10.5 Hz, 1H), 3.86 (m, 1H), 3.82 (dd, J = 2.2
Hz, J = 5.4 Hz, 1H), 3.69 (m, 1H), 3.48 (m, 1H), 3.34 (d, J = 7.9 Hz,
