$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A typical experimental procedure for aldehydes follows: a mixture of
benzaldehyde (1.5 g, 14.1 mmol) in CH3OH (28 mL) was treated with methyl
5-aminovalerate-HCl (2.83 g, 17.0 mmol). TEA (1.86 g, 18.4 mmol) was
added and the mixture was allowed to stir 0.5 h to form die imine. After
treatment with NaBH4 (0.7 g, 18.5 mmol), the reaction mixture was stored
for 19 h at 45 °C. The reaction was worked up as above. The product was
purified by flash column chromatography (EtOAc/OfeCte)to provide the pure
product. Yield 2.4 g 90%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM in-situ generated reactant
