$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: An experimental procedure is illustrated for
the preparation of N-[4-(1-carbethoxy)piperidinyl]-4-nitrobenzenamine
(entry 4): 1-Carbethoxy-4-piperidone (3.2g, 19 mmol), pnitroaniline
(1.4g, 10 mmol) and glacial acetic acid (3.6g, 60 mmol) were mixed in
1,2-dichloroethane (45 mL). Sodium triacetoxyborohydride (6.0g, 28 mmol)
was added to the above solution and the reaction mixture was stirred at
room temperature under a nitrogen atmosphere for 18 h (GC analysis
indicated a complete reaction in addition to ca 20% ketone reduction).
The reaction was quenched with saturated aqueous NaHCO3 and the product
was extracted with EtOAc (3 x 75 mL). The EtOAc extract was dried (MgSO4)
and the solvent was evaporated to give a yellow semi-solid (4.7g). The
semi-solid was washed with ether/hexane (7:3) to remove the piperidone
and piperidol and the solid was collected by filtration (pure by GC). The
analytical sample was obtained by recrystallization from EtOAc/hexane.
Table I. Entry 2, yield 90%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Reductive amination of aldehydes and ketones with weakly basic anilines
using sodium triacetoxyborohydride
