$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the synthesis of Aryl-Prop-2-ynyl-amine or
Alkyl-Prop-2-ynylamine (C): Propargylamine (171μL; 2.5mmol, 1 equiv) and
aldehyde (3mmol; 1.2 equiv) are mixed in dichloromethane (3mL), and then
sodium triacetoxyborohydride (848mg; 4mmol, 1.6 equiv) is added. The
reaction media is stirred under a stream of argon at room temperature for
4 hours. Dichloromethane (20mL) is added and the organic layer is washed
with NaHCO3 5 % (2x20mL), with brine (1x20mL) then with HCl 1N (20mL).
The aqueous layer is then basified with NaOH 1N (30mL) and extracted with
ethyl acetate (2x20mL). The organic layer was washed with brine then
dried over MgSO4 and reduced under pressure to give the desired compound.
Methyl-(4-methyl-benzyl)-prop-2-ynyl-amine (23) was prepared following
the general procedure C using 4-Methyl-benzaldehyde to afford 313 mg
(90%) of Methyl-(4-methyl-benzyl)-prop-2-ynyl-amine as orange oil. LC-MS
(EI(+)): m/z 174 [M+H]+; RT = 2.47 min; 1H NMR (CDCl3): 7.13-7.27 (m,
4H), 3.55 (s, 2H), 3.30 (d, 2H, J=2.4 Hz), 2.35 (s, 3H), 2.28 (t, 1H,
J=2.4 Hz); 13C NMR (CDCl3): 136.9, 135.4, 129.3, 129.1, 78.3, 73.4, 59.8,
44.8, 41.9, 21.3.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
