$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 1H-benzimidazole-2-carboxaldehyde (0.731 g, 5
mmol) was suspended in MeOH (12 mL) and added to a solution of
bis-((2-pyridyl)methyl)amine (0.996 g, 5 mmol) in 1,2-dichloroethane (13
mL). Sodium triacetoxyborohydride, (STAB-H, 95%, 1.673 g, 7.5 mmol) was
added and the reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature. After 48
hours, mass spectrometry analysis of the reaction mixture revealed the
presence of the bis(pyridyl)amine, so an additional portion of aldehyde
(0.292 g, 2 mmol) and STAB-H (1.673 g, 7.5 mmol) were added to the orange
solution. After a further 12 h, the reaction was quenched with saturated
NaHCO3 and the methanol was removed under reduced pressure. The pH of the
aqueous mixture was maintained in the 8-9 range, and the product was
extracted with dichloromethane (3 × 30 mL). The combined organic layers
were washed with water, dried over anhydrous MgSO4, filtered, and
concentrated to dark orange/brown oil. This material was purified by
column chromatography on basic alumina (Acros, Brokmann activity I,
50-200 micron, 250 g, 5.5 × 15 cm2) using ethyl acetate (1.5 L)
containing 1% methanol. Basic alumina TLC plates (RediSep, 254 nm
fluorescent, 1 × 5 cm2) were used to examine each 20-mL fraction eluted
from the column. (Bim)(Py)(Trz), as light orange oil (0.066, 89%).
ESI-MS: m/z 410.2 (M+H+), 432.2 (M+Na+). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.58
(ddd, J = 4.9, 1.8, 0.9 Hz, 1H), 7.62 (td, J = 7.7, 1.8 Hz, 1H), 7.61 -
7.56 (m, 2H), 7.45 (s, 1H), 7.37 (dm, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 7.35 - 7.30 (m,
3H), 7.22 - 7.18 (m, 4H), 7.19 - 7.15 (m, 1H), 5.42 (s, 2H), 3.96 (s,
2H), 3.84 (s, 2H), 3.79 (s, 2H). 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ 158.08,
152.69, 149.13, 144.21, 137.13, 134.53, 129.20, 128.85, 128.14, 124.26,
123.35, 122.70, 122.18, 115.20, 59.37, 54.21, 51.75, 48.60. 14 (Eq. S17).
