$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of 3(R)-1,3-dibenzyl-4-(trifluoroacetyl)piperazin-2-one (6f).
To a 0 °C stirring suspension of D-phenylalanine methyl ester
hydrochloride (100 mg, 0.464 mmol, 1.0 equiv.), 4Å powdered molecular
sieves (200 mg), acetic acid (80 μL, 1.39 mmol, 3.0 equiv.) and sodium
triacetoxyborohydride (148 mg, 0.696 mmol, 1.5 equiv.) in 5 mL
acetonitrile was added dropwise over 5 minutes a 2.5 mL acetonitrile
solution of aldehyde 4f (125 mg, 0.510 mmol, 1.1 equiv.). After stirring
for 90 minutes, the ice bath was removed and the reaction was warmed to
ambient temperature and stirred for 18 hours. The mixture was poured into
aqueous saturated NaHCO3, which was extracted three times with
dichloromethane. The combined organic extracts were dried (Na2SO4),
filtered and concentrated in vacuo. Purification by flash chromatography
(0 to 30% ethyl acetate in hexanes) provided piperazinone 6f as clear oil
(151 mg, 87% yield). Chiral HPLC analysis (Chiralcel OD column 250 X 4.6
mm; 220 nm; flow = 1.0 mL/minute of A/B:80/20 (A=hexanes, B=ethanol); 15
minute run. >99.9% enantiomeric excess. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ
7.36-7.25 (m, 5H), 7.23-7.16 (m, 5H), 5.14 (t, J = 4.9 Hz, 1H), 4.99 (d,
J = 14.6 Hz, 2H), 4.27 (d, J = 14.6 Hz, 2H), 3.65 (br d, J = 15.6 Hz,
1H), 3.58 (dd, J = 13.9, 4.6 Hz, 1H), 3.32 (dd, J = 13.9, 5.2 Hz, 1H),
3.28 (td, J = 12.0, 3.9 Hz, 1H), 2.89 (dt, J = 12.5, 2.9 Hz, 1H), 2.61
(ddd, J = 14.9, 11.7, 3.5 Hz, 1H). HRMS (ES) exact mass calculated for
C20H19F3N2O2Na (M+Na+): 399.1291; found 388.1288.Retention time for 6f =
6.7 minutes (Area % = 97.82), enantiomer retention time = 9.9 minutes
(Area % = 0.03);
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM mol. sieves used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Preparation of Substituted Piperazinones via Tandem Reductive
Amination-(N,N'-Acyl Transfer)-Cyclization
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Beshore, Douglas C.; Dinsmore, Christopher J.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2002), 4(7), 1201-1204

