$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of 3(R)-4-benzoyl-1,3-dibenzylpiperazin-2-one (6e). To a 0 °C
stirring suspension of D-phenylalanine methyl ester hydrochloride (100
mg, 0.464 mmol, 1.0 equiv.), 4Å powdered molecular sieves (200 mg),
acetic acid (80 μL, 1.4 mmol, 3.0 equiv.) and sodium
triacetoxyborohydride (148 mg, 0.696 mmol, 1.5 equiv.) in 5 mL
acetonitrile was added a 2.5 mL acetonitrile solution of aldehyde 4e (129
mg, 0.510 mmol, 1.1 equiv.) dropwise. After stirring for 90 minutes, the
ice bath was removed and the reaction was warmed to ambient temperature
and stirred for 18 hours. The reaction was heated to reflux for 4 hours,
cooled and poured into aqueous saturated NaHCO3, which was extracted
three times with dichloromethane. The combined organic extracts were
dried (Na2SO4), filtered and concentrated in vacuo. Purification by flash
chromatography (0 to 50% ethyl acetate in dichloromethane) provided
piperazinone 6e as clear oil (153 mg, 86% yield). Chiral HPLC analysis
(Chiralcel OD column 250 X 4.6 mm; 220 nm; flow = 1.0 mL/minute of
A/B:75/25 (A=hexanes, B=ethanol); 25 minute run. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3)
δ 7.42-7.14 (m, 14H), 7.13-6.98 (m, 1H), 4.96 (d, J = 14.2 Hz, 1H),
4.76-4.58 (m, 1H), 4.31 (d, J = 14.6 Hz, 1H), 3.68-3.54 (m, 1H),
3.54-3.38 (m, 1H), 3.24-3.00 (m, 2H), 2.75 (br d, J = 11.0 Hz, 1H), 2.56
(br t, J = 12.0 Hz, 1H). HRMS (ES) exact mass calculated for C25H25N2O2
(M+H+): 385.1910; found 385.1914. Retention time for 6e = 12.1 minutes
(Area % = 80.22), enantiomer retention time = 14.0 minutes (Area % = 0);
>99.8% enantiomeric excess.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM mol. sieves used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Preparation of Substituted Piperazinones via Tandem Reductive
Amination-(N,N'-Acyl Transfer)-Cyclization
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Beshore, Douglas C.; Dinsmore, Christopher J.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2002), 4(7), 1201-1204

