$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Experimental for Solid Phase Synthesis of
indinavir: 250 mg of Rapp TentaGel S COOH resin (0.25mmol/g) was added to
a reaction vessel and suspended in 5 ml CH2Cl2/DMF (4:1). The slurry was
treated with 2 (5 eq), EDC (5 eq) and DMAP (2 eq) overnight then filtered
and washed three times each with DMF, 2-propanol and CH2Cl2. To the resin
3 was added 5 ml 30% TFA/CH2Cl2 and the slurry mixed for 1 h then
filtered and washed three times each with CH2Cl2, 10% Et3N/ CH2Cl2,
CH2Cl2. To the resulting resin in 5 ml CH2Cl2/DMF (4:1) was added 4 (2.5
eq), EDC (5 eq), HOBt (5 eq) and Et3N (6 eq). After mixing overnight, the
resin was filtered and washed three times each with DMF, 2-propanol and
CH2Cl2. Resin 5 was suspended in CH2Cl2 (4 ml) and TFA (2 ml) was added.
The mixture was agitated for 0.5 h and then filtered and washed three
times each with CH2Cl2, 10% Et3N/ CH2Cl2, CH2Cl2, DMF. The resulting
resin in 4 ml 1% AcOH/DMF was treated with 6 (10 eq) and NaB(OAc)3H (10
eq) overnight. Then the resin was filtered and washed three times each
with DMF, 2-propanol and CH2Cl2. Resin 7 in 5 ml THF was added
HF/pyridine (0.5 ml) was mixed at rt for 6 h. Then the resin was filtered
and washed three times each with THF, DMF, 2-propanol and CH2Cl2. The
cleavage was performed with 3 ml of 9:1 MeOH/Et3N at 50 °C overnight The
resin was removed by filtration and the sample was concentrated to
dryness. Entry j, yield 86% HPLC Purity: 81%
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, RESIN SUPPORTED REACTION
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Solid Phase Synthesis of Indinavir and Its Analogues
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Cheng, Yuan; Lu, Zhijian; Chapman, Kevin T.; Tata, James R.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Combinatorial Chemistry (2000), 2(5), 445-446

