$DATUM Chiral Boc-diamine.
2-Amino-2'-hydroxy-6'-trifluoromethyl-1,1'-binaphthalene (8) (684 mg,
1.93 mmol) and sodium triacetoxyborohydride (818 mg, 3.86 mmol) were
added as solids to a 50 mL round-bottom flask and suspended in 19 mL of
1,2-dichloroethane. A solution of
N-(tert-butyloxycarbonyl)-N-(formylmethyl)-2,4,6-trimethylphenylamine3
(642 mg, 2.32 mmol) in 1,2-dichloroethane (8 mL) was then introduced
dropwise over a period of 1 h by a gas-tight syringe. After 1 h of
additional stirring, the mixture was diluted with saturated aqueous
solution of NaHCO3 (50 mL) and CH2Cl2 (50 mL). The isolated aqueous layer
was washed twice with CH2Cl2 (50 mL). The combined organic layers were
dried over MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated. Purification by silica gel
chromatography in 2:1 hexanes: Et2O delivered the protected diamine as a
white foam (1.02 g, 1.66 mmol, 86%). In CDCl3 at 25 °C, this material
exists as a 4:1 mixture of amide rotamers. (R f = 0.26). IR (neat): 3383
(br), 3056 (w), 2987 (m), 2930 (m), 2861 (w), 1688 (s), 1618 (s), 1599
(s), 1479 (s), 1394 (s), 1367 (s), 1313 (s), 1206 (s), 1178 (s), 1150
(s), 1123 (s). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.16-8.11 (m, 1H), 7.98 (d, 8.8
Hz, 1H), 7.92 (d, J = 9.0 Hz, 1H), 7.81-7.76 (m, 1H), 7.45 (d, J = 8.9
Hz, 1H), 7.42-7.32 (m, 1H), 7.27-7.14 (m, 3H), 6.88-6.75 (m, 2H), 5.34
(s, 1H), 5.27 (s, 1H), 4.25 (br, 1H), 3.71-3.58 (m, 1H), 3.42-3.30 (m,
3H), 2.23 (s, 3H), 2.20 (s, minor 3H), 2.08 (s, minor 3H), 2.06 (s, minor
3H), 2.03 (s, 3H), 1.98 (s, 3H), 1.49 (s, minor 9H), 1.15 (s, 9H). 13C
NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 155.6, 154.1, 145.2, 144.9, 137.5, 137.2, 136.7,
135.7, 135.4, 135.3, 135.2, 134.3, 131.4, 131.3, 129.6, 129.2, 129.1,
128.5, 127.7, 127.6, 127.5, 126.3 (q, J = 4.6 Hz), 125.7, 125.6, 125.4,
123.3, 122.7, 122.5, 122.3, 119.3,119.3,114.7, 113.6, 113.5, 106.7, 80.6,
79.8,49.0, 42.8, 34.8,31.7,28.6,28.2, 25.4, 22.8, 21.0,18.1, 17.9,14.2.
