$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure A for the Reductive
Amination of Tetrabutylammonium(Formylaryl)trifluoroborates using
Palladium-Catalyzed Formate. Tetrabutylammonium
(4-((Piperidin-1-yl)methyl)furan-2-yl)trifluoroborate. A test tube
containing activated 4 Å molecular sieves and tetrabutylammonium
(4-formylfuran-2-yl)trifluoroborate was evacuated under vacuum (0.01
Torr) for 15 min. DMF (1 mL), piperidine (60 mg, 0.71mmol), and formic
acid (28 mg, 0.61 mmol) were then added with stirring. The solution was
heated under nitrogen for 5 h at 70 °C, after which potassium formate
(100 mg, 1.19 mmol) and palladiumacetate (5 mg, 0.02 mmol, 6 mol %) were
added, and stirring was continued for an additional 4 h. Heat was
removed, and the reaction mixture was cooled to room temperature. Aqueous
KHF2 (1 mL,4.5 M) was then added, and the solution was stirred for 20
min. The mixture was filtered, and the white solid was rinsed with CH2Cl2
(2 x 5 mL). The filtrate was washed with H2O, 3 M NaOH, and brine, and
dried (MgSO4), and the solvent was removed to give the product.
Tetrabutylammonium 5-((Piperidin-1-yl)methyl)furan-2-yltrifluoroborate as
a deep yellow oil, yield 159 mg, 86%. IR = 2933, 1669 cm-1; 1H NMR (500
MHz, CDCl3): δ 0.89 (t, J = 8 Hz, 12H), 1.24 - 1.34 (m, 10H), 1.43 - 1.51
(m, 12H), 2.34 (s, 4H), 3.05 (t, J = 9 Hz, 8H), 3.42 (s, 2H), 5.94 (d, J
= 3 Hz, 1H), 6.15 (d, J = 3 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (125.8 MHz, CDCl3): δ 13.6,
19.5, 23.7, 24.2, 26.1, 53.9, 56.0, 58.3, 107.8, 111.7, 151.0; 19F NMR
(471 MHz, CDCl3): δ -141.2; 11B NMR(128 MHz, CDCl3): δ 0.16; HRMS (ESI):
calcd for C10H14BF3NO [M-C16H36N] - 232.1121, found 232.1131.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM molecular sieves used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Functionalization of Organotrifluoroborates: Reductive Amination
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Molander, Gary A.; Cooper, David J.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2008), 73(10), 3885-3891

